    <briefdescription>
<para>Implementation of the process-wide database schema cache declared in <ref refid="databaseschema_8hpp" kindref="compound">databaseschema.hpp</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file defines the single shared schema map and the functions that manage it: the constructor that fills it for every table at startup, populateSchema() that loads one table&apos;s columns, getDatabaseSchema() that hands out a read-only view of the map, and printSchema() that logs its contents. Failures while reading the schema are treated as fatal at startup.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This is where the schema snapshot that <ref refid="classValidator" kindref="compound">Validator</ref> relies on is actually built. <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref>&apos;s constructor creates a <ref refid="classDatabaseSchema" kindref="compound">DatabaseSchema</ref> object, which uses <ref refid="classDatabaseController" kindref="compound">DatabaseController</ref> to discover tables and columns and stores them here. Without this file the cache would be empty, so validation could not run and every request would need a live database schema query.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Static data members / storage duration: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/storage_duration">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/storage_duration</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
